I ascended not too long ago for the first time, and after hearing about
how someone ascended with a tame pestilence, I decided to try playing
healers (I've never had the Staff, and it intrigues me). After a little
bit of that, I got tired of playing a combat wombat healer (never got
very far), and so decided to completely play as a pacifist (which is
very new for me).

So on my second good game of trying out the whole pacifist thing, I
actually got off to a very good start.

I had a pet cat who stayed alive and helped me get down to the second
level of the gnomish mines where I was greeted by w00f the little dog
-- sweet! A bones pile!

I walked over to the loot pile and *blam* -- "you are blinded by a
flash of light". I'm like, "Aaah -- so that's why he died!" Note to
self: Search next to loot piles before brazenly walking onto them.

Well, I'm a gnome and peaceful with most things plus I've got a beefy
cat nearby, so I'm not too worried. I had quaffed my only blessed ! of
EH earlier, and it raised my HP up to 20. The monster that spawned took
me down to 12 or so, so I was a little worried, but not deathly so. I
checked a potion spoiler and was glad to know that a !oH cures
blindness, so I quaffed one of my 3 remaining healing potions and was
able to see that the monsters attacking me were no big deal. I dusted E
(as I did hundreds of times in this game) and was able to scare off the
monsters until m30w and w00f could kill them.

Out of the bones pile I got some good stuff including an uncursed +2
elven cloak -- sweet!

Well continued down some more, got another kitten which I named m3w,
though she promptly stepped onto a level teleporter and I'm not sure
what happened to w00f. So just m30w and I descended into minetown.

One oil lamp in Izchak's -- nothing else but candles.

Cross-aligned altar, and I was able to donate for 6 points of
protection before I realized that I should have credit-cloned my money
before donating it. Shoot! I'm still new at this whole credit-cloning
business, I normally RP as lawful in my games, but promised myself to
use every trick in the book if I can ascend pacifist.

Went over to the toolshop and found two lamps (!), both of which were
magic (!!!). I think m30w stole one, and I bought the other. I took
them over to the altar -- one was uncursed, and the other was blessed.
Go RNG! :)

So that magic lamp promptly turned into an oil lamp and I was burdened
by my brand-new +2 GDSM. yay! I dropped my old leather armor and was
unburdened, and had about -14 AC. Rock on! This game's not turning out
so bad at all!

So I wandered around having m30w kill things for a while and eventually
she was at around level 9 with 60 HP or so -- she was doing pretty
good, quite capable of soloing the watchmen (which she did).

I cloned enough credit to clean out all of the shops (including
Izchak's -- but I left him alive) of gold, and donated down to 0 or -1
(forget which) naked AC and about 2000 turns of clairvoyance, and kept
about 600 so that I could buy my Oracularities.

Here's where I was feeling pretty good.

So m30w and I head down another level and I was greeted by a kitten.
Cool! Tamed it with a candy bar and after levelling up the newly
christened Snuggles, I was shocked to have m30w hit a trap door. Aaah!
Hurriedly descended to find her (phew -- only 1 level down) and then
found m3w again (but didn't have anything to tame her with except my
last food ration, and I had negative luck from accidentally eating a
gnome so I thought it was wise to save my food). Descended again and
was greeted by a peaceful gnome lord deliberately jumping onto a poly
trap and turning into a peaceful woodland elf. Sweet! Identified poly
trap!

So I promptly started poly'ing my pets -- soon, m30w was soon a baby
silver dragon and Snuggles was a bone devil, then a giant eel.

Then, a Bad Thing happened. A hobgoblin played a fire horn from about 6
squares away, and hit me, then it burned my boots, which took my HP
from 20 to 0, while I had -18 AC. *sigh*.

If you say I should have wished for SDSM instead -- well, maybe that
would have saved me, but I think GDSM was the right choice given the
circumstances. Arguably, I should have gone to the Oracle right after
doing my protection racket, but that's about the only thing I can think
of I should have known better to do differently.

*sigh*. <loads up another game>



